  "answer": "**Final status: passing.** `make build && make unit && make component` exits 0: the build has 0 errors, unit tests pass 272/272 and component tests pass 20/20. It took one fix attempt, then two confirmation runs.\n\n**What failed:** `make build` and `make component` were fine. `make unit` had 39 of 272 tests failing, all in `SemanticMatcherTests`, each with an error like `Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'`.\n\n**Root cause:** In `src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs`, the method that reads a matcher spec lowercased the name before looking it up. The built-in matchers are stored under their exact names (`isUuid`, `isIsoDateTime`, `greaterThan`, \u2026), and that lookup is case-sensitive. So `isUuid` became `isuuid`, matched nothing, and every built-in matcher was rejected as unknown. Custom matchers registered through `SuiteConfig.CustomMatchers` with mixed-case names would have failed the same way.\n\n**What changed:** I removed the two lowercasing calls in that method (`SemanticMatcher.cs:85` and `:91`), so names are now matched exactly as written. No tests were changed. I checked first that no test expects matcher names to work regardless of case.\n\n**One unexplained run:** In one confirmation run where I hid all the output, the chain exited with code 2 and I couldn't see which step failed. Every run since passed: all three targets one at a time, and the full command chain end to end. It looks like a one-off, but I don't know what caused it.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
